\par }{\b \hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 8.1 Select your game controller based on its characteristics on Control Options screen
\par }{\hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 When playing Motocross Madness 2, you need to\hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1  select your game controller on the Control Options screen based on its characteristics (.e.g., \ldblquote 2-axis, 4+ button joystick,\rdblquote  
\ldblquote standard game pad,\rdblquote  \ldblquote mouse,\rdblquote  etc.) When you choose a controller type from the list of presets, key driving and stunt controls ar\hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 e\hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 
 assigned to axes or buttons on your controller. You can also customize the button and control assignments for your controller on the Control Options screen.}{\b 
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 8.2 Note on dual analog game controllers (inc. Hammerhead FX game pad)
\par }{\hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 You can use a dual analog \hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 
game controller with Motocross Madness 2, but there are some limitations to how you can assign controls. Steering and leaning can be mapped to the left thumbstick, but only acceleration can be mapped to the right thumbstick. When acceleration is mapped to
\hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1  \hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 the right thumbstick, acceleration is either on or off; there is no gradation of throttle input. Also, please note that you cannot map braking control to an axis.
\par 
\par }{\b \hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 8.3 If joystick response feels jittery
\par }{\hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 If you are using a joystick to play Motocross Madness\hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 
 2, and the joystick response feels jittery, turning on the Filter Joystick Input checkbox (on the Advanced Options screen) may reduce the jittery feel. Please note that it may also affect driving controls.
\par 
\par }{\b \hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 8.4 Do not switch game controllers while a game is in progress
\par }{\hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 If you want to switch your game controller (e.g., unplug a joystick and replace it with a game pad), do so before you start Motocross Madness 2. If you switch controllers while the game is runn\hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 
ing, it may not recognize all commands correctly.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s22\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f15\fs20\cgrid {\hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 8.5 USB controllers are not detected unless they are identified by Windows Device Manager with Controller I.D. #1.
\par }{\b0 \hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 To confirm that your USB controller is assigned Controller I.D. #1, click the Start button\hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 
, point to Settings, click Control Panel, and then double-click Game Controllers. Click the Advanced tab. You may need to physically remove any non-USB controllers from your computer in order to allow your USB controller to use Controller ID #1.
\par }{
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 8.6 Multi\hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 ple controllers connected to your computer
\par }\pard\plain \widctlpar\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {\hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 
If you have more than one game controller plugged into your computer (e.g., one plugged into a gameport and the other to a USB port), Motocross Madness 2 will only recognize the gameport controller. For Motocross \hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 
Madness to recognize the USB controller, you must disconnect the other controller from the gameport, delete it from the list of devices in the Game Controllers applet (on the Control Panel), and then assign the USB controller Controller ID #1.
\par 
\par }{\b \hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 8.7 No forc\hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 e-feedback effects when using a force-feedback-enabled joystick
\par }{\hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 If your joystick\rquote s force-feedback effects are not working in Motocross Madness 2 after you\rquote ve selected the joystick as your controller, you may need to quit and then restart Motocross Madness 
\hich\af1\dbch\af16\loch\f1 2 to turn on force-feedback effects.
\par 
